gideon (0.1.0-2) noble; urgency=medium

  * Wrapper now prepends $HOME/.local/bin to PATH. The systemd user manager
    omits it, so the tray's LLM start/stop control could not find an ollama
    installed there and failed with "'ollama' not found on PATH". Answering
    was unaffected - that goes over HTTP to a running instance.
  * preinst/postinst no longer warn about a missing ollama when the invoking
    user has one in ~/.local/bin; they run as root, whose PATH excludes it.

 -- Ankit Chhetri <achhetri@webmd.net>  Sat, 05 Sep 2026 04:45:00 +0000

gideon (0.1.0-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian packaging.
  * Fully offline install: bundles a relocatable CPython 3.12, all 51 runtime
    Python distributions, PortAudio and the Ayatana AppIndicator stack, plus
    every model weight (faster-whisper small, Piper en_US-lessac-high,
    openWakeWord feature extractors and the custom hey_gideon wake word).
    Nothing is downloaded at install time.
  * Installs as a systemd user service, enabled for all users via
    `systemctl --global enable`.
  * Requires a local Ollama instance for the language-model step; this is the
    one component not bundled. See README.Debian.

 -- Ankit Chhetri <achhetri@webmd.net>  Sat, 05 Sep 2026 04:00:00 +0000
